Subject: [EXPERIMENT] drm/amd/pm: trace Polaris SMU startup and firmware lookup

Local diagnostic against Linux6.12.113-1; no hardware acceptance.
Report firmware selection and existing register state without changing reset
sequencing or suppressing failures. Propagate failed CGS firmware lookup.
No firmware payload dumps, raw PCI writes or alternative clock settings.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_cgs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_cgs.c
@@ -414,6 +414,7 @@
 				return -EINVAL;
 			}
 
+			dev_info(adev->dev, "SMU_DIAG firmware=%s\n", fw_name);
 			err = amdgpu_ucode_request(adev, &adev->pm.fw, "%s", fw_name);
 			if (err) {
 				DRM_ERROR("Failed to load firmware \"%s\"", fw_name);
@@ -443,6 +444,10 @@
 		info->image_size = ucode_size;
 		info->ucode_start_address = ucode_start_address;
 		info->kptr = (void *)src;
+		dev_info(adev->dev, "SMU_DIAG version=%08x bytes=%u offset=%u start=%08x\n",
+			 info->version, info->image_size,
+			 le32_to_cpu(hdr->header.ucode_array_offset_bytes),
+			 info->ucode_start_address);
